From 853ba53021d23ab301fef75d16328f25796a8a3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Caleb J. Westfall" <calebwestfall1989@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:55:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] SOTA-4: one-process CJCS engine, held-out checksum forensics
 and repair, soundness audit, pilot infrastructure

- proofscope/experimental/cjcs4.py + lean/ProofScope/CJCSSearch.lean: the SOTA-3 CJCS algorithm
  (same obligations, portfolios, heartbeat budget and verdict mapping) searched in ONE Lean REPL
  environment per pair; proposals verified by a fresh lean compile, the unchanged axiom rule and
  leanchecker replay (fail closed). Exact `first` alternative selection via success markers.
- bench/sota4/integrity.py + research/cjcs/*.MANIFEST.json: canonical-JSON manifests computed from the
  authenticated original bytes; the SOTA-3 gate failure is one appended LF per file (bb8628b6
  reproduced byte-for-byte). Held-out set unchanged.
- bench/sota4/{measure,specs,failures,report}.py: case-level measurement with Lean launch shims,
  SOTA-3 failure classification (original records preserved), machine-readable reports.
- bench/runner.py: adds system cjcs4 only.
- research/cjcs/sota4_hostile + tests/sota4: hostile pairs and adversarial controls.
- bench/pilot: blinded two-reviewer labelling, kappa, adjudication, conflict refusal (no labels).
- docs/sota4: report (status INCONCLUSIVE pending the Mathlib measurement), integrity, soundness
  audit, mathematical limits, pilot protocol, local evidence including superseded slower builds.
- .github/workflows/sota4-research.yml.

No state-of-the-art claim; development evidence only.

